  "final_message": "The root cause was in `collect` in `billing/payments.py`. When a customer had no default payment method, it returned `None` without calling `record_failure`. So no attempt was counted, no retry was scheduled, no `invoice.payment_failed` event was emitted, and the subscription never moved to `past_due`.\n\nThe fix is to call `record_failure(ctx, invoice, \"no_payment_method\")` before that early return. This puts the invoice on the same path as the expired-card case. The 24 existing tests pass. I didn't add a test for the no-payment-method case, and I didn't run mypy.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` in the repo root: `{\"file\": \"payments.py\", \"function\": \"collect\"}`.",
